    "filmNote": "Made once in Google Flow on 2 November 2026 (ayodhya/opening/flow, NOTES.md): a Nano Banana Pro first frame of the Saryu ghats at night with the Ram Mandir across the river, unlit, the ghat steps lined with unlit diyas and one diya floating close to the camera; a Veo 3.1 Fast clip from that first frame alone (Kamal's lesson), in which the diyas light in a wave from the near steps round the curve and away, then the temple lights tier by tier, and the camera rises a little. Downloaded at 1080p, its last 1.2 s eased to a stop (tools/easeout.py), cropped to the 9:16 window clear of Flow's marks (tools/process_film.py). The last frame is the film's own; the names are written in the sky above the temple. Glints in code bloom over the temple tiers and the lit ghat steps (opening.glints); a Flow extension tried as a looping film drifted sideways and was not kept.",
